  id: Gastrocnemius_muscle.L
  partName: Gastrocnemius_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The gastrocnemius is a large and powerful muscle responsible for extending the
    hock and flexing the knee. It plays a critical role in propulsion, especially
    during running and jumping. '
  - This muscle generates significant force, allowing strong push-off from the ground.
    It also contributes to stability and coordination of the hindlimb. Working with
    the common calcaneal tendon, it ensures efficient transfer of force during movement.
